{
 "summary": "Removes AssumeUTXO snapshot loading, background historical validation, and multi-chainstate infrastructure across Bitcoin Core. Consolidates ChainstateManager, BlockManager, and validation notification interfaces to manage a single active chainstate, retiring dual block-file cursors, separate historical block downloads, dynamic cache rebalancing, and the loadtxoutset RPC. Rejects existing datadirs containing incomplete snapshots at initialization, while retaining UTXO snapshot dumping via dumptxoutset.",
 "problem": "Managing concurrent chainstates adds pervasive complexity throughout validation, database lifetimes, cache rebalancing, P2P block syncing, pruning, and wallet rescans. The author argues this complexity is no longer justified given low real-world adoption, trust ambiguities in background sync, and recent performance gains in ordinary initial block download.",
 "evidence": [
  "PR description: 'Multiple chainstates affect much more than snapshot loading: ordinary validation changes have to account for different chainstate roles, candidate sets, notifications, downloads, pruning, cache allocation, database lifetimes and locks. I am not sure this amount of complexity in the most critical part of our codebase is still worth it, given that adoption isn't where we hoped it would be.'",
  "PR description notes ordinary IBD speedups reducing the need for snapshots: '#35295 is already merged, and the upcoming pruneassumevalid will make pruned IBD even faster.'"
 ],
 "dependencies": {
  "depends_on": [
   "#36601"
  ],
